# What `docker build` may NOT read from this directory. The image built from
# docker/Dockerfile runs `pnpm build:ci` and `pnpm e2e`, and the reason it
# exists is that those two must never see the database `.env.local` names
# (docs/adr/0003-builds-and-e2e-run-in-docker.md). A file listed here is never
# sent to the Docker daemon, so it cannot end up in the image.
#
# src/docker-policy.spec.ts fails the gate if a line below is removed, and if
# a `!` line is added to re-include anything.

# Secret-bearing files — AGENTS.md hard constraint #2. The `**` forms cover
# nested directories; a bare pattern only matches at the context root.
.env*
**/.env*
**/.envrc
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_*
**/.aws
**/.npmrc
.vercel

# Other checkouts (`.claude/worktrees/` holds whole ones, with their own
# ignored files) and the repository's full history.
.claude
.git

# The host's dependencies and build are for the host's OS; the image installs
# and builds its own.
**/node_modules
.next
next-env.d.ts
public/sw.js
public/sw.js.map
*.tsbuildinfo

# Run output and local state.
coverage
media
test-results
playwright-report
e2e-server.log
test-results.xml
.superpowers
**/.DS_Store
